menuconfig ZMK_FEATURE_BRAILLE
    bool "Braille input module"
    default n
    depends on !ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      Build the out-of-tree Braille behavior module on the split central
      or a non-split keyboard. Braille dot/space behaviors route input by
      binding parameter on any layer, without an on/off state. Chords collect
      all nine Braille bits until the last release, without a timer. The mode
      key composes ZMK hold-tap/layer behaviors; settings hooks suspend Braille
      typing until exit. The shared engine matches the selected mode's tables
      and dispatches host keystrokes; the ueb1 table carries the 26 six-dot
      alphabet cells as lowercase letters. Literary signs, real factory
      command chords, context transitions, the settings UI, and persistence
      are not implemented yet.

if ZMK_FEATURE_BRAILLE

config ZMK_BRAILLE_GRADE2
    bool "Optional UEB Grade 2 rules"
    default n
    help
      Include the optional Grade 2 rule-data translation unit. It is currently
      a placeholder, not a working contracted Braille table. The initial
      feature set does not require it.

endif # ZMK_FEATURE_BRAILLE
